==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Bazibon''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bazibastra''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Bazifenix''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Bazibon is essentially the [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] counterpart to [[Strike Unit R.E.I. (Uber Rare Cat)|Strike Unit R.E.I.]] and [[Pai-Pai (Uber Rare Cat)|Pai-Pai]]. This unit is amazing in [[Cats of the Cosmos]] in its Evolved and True Forms. With its Warp immunity and ability to break every single [[Barrier]] it hits, it trivializes two big challenges.

Bazibon's Massive Damage and Resistance to Aliens can be a lethal combo in both [[Into the Future]] and [[Cats of the Cosmos]], as it outranges the majority of the Aliens found there. Even if they get close or outrange, Bazibon can still tank a few hits before getting knocked back or taking its targets out. Its performance increases immensely as it breezes through these chapters and helps the player acquire more anti-Alien treasures.

However, against non-Aliens, Bazibon is rather squishy, so proper meatshielding is recommended. As its stats are rather average and its range is mediocre for an Uber Rare, it is not advised to use any of Bora's forms against non-Aliens unless you have no alternatives for generalist offense. Even in mixed stages featuring some Aliens, Bazibon can struggle to last long enough to hit its intended targets.

==='''True Form'''===
Bazibastra gets improved health and attack. Firstly, the improved attack is good as it allows it to stand on a passable level of DPS for an Uber against non-Aliens for its range. However, better alternatives are aplenty. Against Aliens, however, its damage improvement puts Bazibastra as one of the highest DPS among all Alien nukers. The improved health increases its survivability against non-Aliens mainly. The health improvement is also good for Aliens as well, just less noticeable. The extra health also gives it an easier time lasting long enough for its relatively short cooldown to end for another to enter the battle.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
With even higher attack power and range, Bazifenix's role changes from a midranged nuker to a backliner nuker. This increase in DPS is always welcome, and its increased range is extremely helpful for its survivability. Its weaken ability is marginally helpful, as any Alien that manages to survive its tremendous '''343,040''' damage will be crippled to 50% at a ~60% uptime. This form comes at a cost of two Blue Gems, however, which has better usages in other areas. If you happen to have two spare Gems and ten Blue Catfruit, not to mention 15 Dark Catseyes, however, this form is definitely powerful, but the fact that it is extremely expensive makes it low on the priority list for Ultra Forms. If you have the materials to spare, however, and you get this form, consider most Alien stages in the game free.

==='''Talents'''===
The most notable Talents are '''Strengthen''' and '''Weaken Resist'''. The former allows Bazibastra to accumulate even more massive amounts of DPS against Aliens and supports its generalist usage against non-Aliens as well. The Weaken Resist is useful for Aliens only, as a lot of Alien enemies have a very powerful weaken ability. Examples include [[Calamary]] and [[LeMurr]]. Getting the Weaken Resist will help it recover sooner from such events, being able to dish out massive DPS once more.

Improvements to '''Health''' and '''Attack''' are welcome as well, considering how this unit makes use of both. Combining these Talents with Catseye boosts can make this unit absolutely shine like a supernova against Aliens. These Talents are definitely overkill for most of the game, though late-game Aliens can often be buffed to ridiculous extents.

'''Slow Resist''', on the other hand, is very situational and will not bring any notable change. It could possibly help against [[Galactic Overseer Nyandam]] and [[Super Hyppoh]]. However, this Talent is nowhere near as useful for [[Imperator Sael]] and [[Queen B]], since Bazibastra can outrange the former for quick destruction and infiltrate the blindspot of the latter with proper timing for more quick destruction. This Talent also suffers from simply reducing the duration of Slow instead of outright negating Slow.

